<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sidoarjo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sidoarjo is a town and regency in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brantas-river">Brantas</a> delta just south of Surabaya. The fertile delta was the heartland of the 11th-century kingdom of Janggala. Today the area is an industrial and fishpond district, known also for the Lusi mud volcano, which erupted in 2006 and buried several villages.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sidoarjo.jpg" alt="Sidoarjo" width="320" height="171" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://www.wisatasidoarjo.com · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alun-alun-sidoarjo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
